@host = http://localhost:5000

### Health
GET {{host}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### List: defaults (page 1, 20 items, newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/requests
Accept: application/json

### List: filter by status + priority
GET {{host}}/api/requests?status=Waiting&priority=High
Accept: application/json

### List: combined filter (status, organization, date range)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?status=InProgress&organizationName=עיריית חיפה&createdFrom=2025-01-01&createdTo=2026-06-30
Accept: application/json

### List: search in Hebrew (Title or OrganizationName contains)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?search=תלונה
Accept: application/json

### List: search by organization text
GET {{host}}/api/requests?search=המרכז הרפואי
Accept: application/json

### List: date range (inclusive of both days)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?createdFrom=2026-01-01&createdTo=2026-01-31
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by createdAt asc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=createdAt&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by createdAt desc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=createdAt&sortDirection=desc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by updatedAt asc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=updatedAt&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by updatedAt desc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=updatedAt&sortDirection=desc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by priority asc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=priority&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by priority desc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=priority&sortDirection=desc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by title asc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=title&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by title desc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=title&sortDirection=desc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by organizationName asc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=organizationName&sortDirection=asc
Accept: application/json

### List: sort by organizationName desc
GET {{host}}/api/requests?sortBy=organizationName&sortDirection=desc
Accept: application/json

### List: page 2
GET {{host}}/api/requests?page=2&pageSize=20
Accept: application/json

### Invalid: pageSize=500 (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?pageSize=500
Accept: application/json

### Invalid: status=Banana (expect 400)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?status=Banana
Accept: application/json

### Get by id
GET {{host}}/api/requests/1
Accept: application/json

### Get by id that does not exist (expect 404)
GET {{host}}/api/requests/999999
Accept: application/json

### Stats over all requests
GET {{host}}/api/requests/stats
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Status update. First GET the request and copy its "version" into @version below; the client must always
# send the version it last saw. Request 1 is Completed in the seeded data, so use an open request, e.g. from
# GET {{host}}/api/requests?status=InProgress&pageSize=1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@requestId = 2
@version = AAAAAAAAB9E=

### Get the current state (copy "version" from the response)
GET {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}
Accept: application/json

### Successful status change (expect 200 with the new status and a new version)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: dana.levi

{ "newStatus": "Waiting", "version": "{{version}}" }

### The same request again with the old version (expect 409 with "current")
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: dana.levi

{ "newStatus": "Completed", "version": "{{version}}" }

### Invalid transition: Completed -> New (request 1 is Completed; copy its version first; expect 400)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "New", "version": "AAAAAAADGCc=" }

### Invalid status value (expect 400)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Banana", "version": "{{version}}" }

### Malformed version (expect 400)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Waiting", "version": "not-a-version" }

### Non-existing id (expect 404)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/999999/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress", "version": "AAAAAAAAB9E=" }

### History of a request, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/history
Accept: application/json
